---
const headingId = "fridge-measurement-resource";
---

<section class="measurement-resource" aria-labelledby={headingId}>
  <h2 id={headingId}>Measure the opening, door space and delivery route</h2>
  <p>
    Start with the space in your kitchen, then compare it with the installation guide for
    the exact fridge. Check the room needed around it, how far the doors must open and
    whether the delivery team can get it into place.
  </p>
  <div class="measurement-diagrams">
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/fridge-opening.svg"
        alt="Front view of a tall fridge: A marks the finished opening width and B marks the height from the floor to the cupboard above."
        width="560"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Measure the finished opening.</strong> Check width and height at the front,
        middle and rear, and write down the smallest measurements. Measure usable depth
        separately, allowing for skirting, trim and anything behind the fridge.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/fridge-door-clearance.svg"
        alt="Top view of a fridge beside a wall: A marks the hinge-side gap, a curved line shows the door swing, and a drawer extends into the room."
        width="560"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Check the doors beside walls.</strong> Use the model's required wall gap
        and door angle. Make sure you can fully pull out the drawers and remove them
        for cleaning. A door opening to 90 degrees does not guarantee drawer access.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="delivery-diagram">
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/fridge-delivery-route.svg"
        alt="A tall fridge carton labelled width, height and depth, beside a top view of a delivery route through a doorway and around a corner."
        width="560"
        height="480"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Measure the whole delivery route.</strong> Check the packaged size against
        every doorway, tight turn, stairway and lift. Ask the delivery team to confirm
        access, including any need to unpack, remove doors or tilt the fridge.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="diagram-note">Original Australian Home Collective diagrams. Illustrative only, not to scale; shaded gaps and door angles do not set the requirements for your fridge.</p>
  <div class="measurement-download">
    <div>
      <h3>Take the measurements with you</h3>
      <p>Use the free one-page A4 worksheet to record your kitchen opening, fridge dimensions, ventilation gaps and delivery checks. Leave unknown measurements blank until confirmed.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href="/downloads/fridge-measurement-worksheet.pdf" download data-measurement-download="fridge">
      Download fridge worksheet (PDF)
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .measurement-resource { margin: 2.5rem 0; }
  .measurement-diagrams { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.35rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.8rem; }
  figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #d5e1dc; border-radius: 12px; }
  .delivery-diagram { grid-column: 1 / -1; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; justify-self: center; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #263b3e; }
  figcaption strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .measurement-resource .diagram-note { font-size: 0.85rem; color: #4c625b; line-height: 1.5; }
  .measurement-download { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding: 1.4rem; background: #f0f5f2; border: 1px solid #d5e1dc; border-radius: 14px; }
  .measurement-download h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .measurement-download p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .measurement-download .button { max-width: 100%; white-space: normal; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .measurement-diagrams { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.6rem; } .measurement-download { padding: 1.1rem; } }
  @media print { .measurement-resource { break-inside: auto; } figure { break-inside: avoid; } .measurement-download { background: white; } }
</style>
